│ Okay, let’s address this. I’ve analyzed the  │
│ issue and the provided code context. The     │
│ core problem is that the CheckboxInput       │
│ widget, when rendering a SplitArrayField     │
│ with boolean data, incorrectly sets the      │
│ checked attribute to True after encountering │
│ the first True value in the array. This is   │
│ due to how get_context() modifies the attrs  │
│ dictionary.                                  │
│                                              │
│ Reasoning:                                   │
│                                              │
│ The CheckboxInput’s get_context() method is  │
│ responsible for populating the attrs         │
│ dictionary, which contains attributes passed │
│ to the widget. Specifically, the checked     │
│ attribute is being set to True               │
│ unconditionally after the first True value   │
│ is encountered. This is not the intended     │
│ behavior, as the checked state should        │
│ reflect the actual boolean values in the     │
│ array. The fix involves preventing the       │
│ attrs['checked'] setting after the first     │
│ True value.                                  │
│                                              │
│ Patch:                                       │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  # modification 1                            │
│  [file]django/forms/widgets.py[/file]        │
│  [original]def get_context(self, name):      │
│      context = super().get_context(name)     │
│      if name == 'attrs':                     │
│          attrs = context['attrs']            │
│          for i, value in                     │
│  enumerate(self.data):                       │
│              if value:                       │
│                  attrs['checked'] = True     │
│                  break[/original]            │
│  [patched]def get_context(self, name):       │
│      context = super().get_context(name)     │
│      if name == 'attrs':                     │
│          attrs = context['attrs']            │
│          first_true_found = False            │
│          for i, value in                     │
│  enumerate(self.data):                       │
│              if value:                       │
│                  first_true_found = True     │
│                  break                       │
│          if first_true_found:                │
│              attrs['checked'] =              │
│  True[/patched]                              │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│ Explanation of the Patch:                    │
│                                              │
│ The patch modifies the get_context method    │
│ within the CheckboxInput class. It           │
│ introduces a first_true_found boolean        │
│ variable to track whether a True value has   │
│ been encountered in the self.data array. The │
│ loop now checks if first_true_found is False │
│ before setting attrs['checked'] to True.     │
│ This ensures that attrs['checked'] is only   │
│ set to True after the first True value has   │
│ been found, resolving the issue.             │
