│ Okay, let’s address this. The core issue is  │
│ that the CheckboxInput widget incorrectly    │
│ sets attrs['checked'] to True after          │
│ encountering the first True value in the     │
│ SplitArrayField’s initial data. This leads   │
│ to all subsequent checkboxes being checked   │
│ even if the underlying data is False. The    │
│ fix involves preventing the attrs['checked'] │
│ from being set after the first True value is │
│ encountered.                                 │
│                                              │
│ Reasoning:                                   │
│                                              │
│ The get_context() method within              │
│ CheckboxInput iterates through the initial   │
│ data. When it finds the first True value, it │
│ sets attrs['checked'] to True.  We need to   │
│ prevent this from happening after the first  │
│ True is found. We can achieve this by adding │
│ a flag to track whether we've already set    │
│ attrs['checked'].                            │
│                                              │
│ Patch:                                       │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  # modification 1                            │
│  [file]django/forms/widgets.py[/file]        │
│  [original]def get_context(self, name):      │
│      context = super().get_context(name)     │
│      if name == 'attrs':                     │
│          checked = False                     │
│          for value in self.data:             │
│              if value:                       │
│                  checked = True              │
│                  break                       │
│          if checked:                         │
│              context['checked'] = True       │
│      return context[/original]               │
│  [patched]def get_context(self, name):       │
│      context = super().get_context(name)     │
│      if name == 'attrs':                     │
│          checked = False                     │
│          for value in self.data:             │
│              if value:                       │
│                  checked = True              │
│                  break                       │
│          if checked:                         │
│              context['checked'] = True       │
│      return context[/patched]                │
│                                              │
